---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = new Date("2026-11-21");

const googleAnalyticsCookies = [
  { name: "_ga", purpose: "Distinguishes visitors with a random ID.", expires: "2 years" },
  { name: "_ga_<ID>", purpose: "Keeps track of the current visit (session).", expires: "2 years" },
];

const clarityCookies = [
  {
    name: "_clck",
    party: "First-party",
    purpose: "Keeps a random Clarity user ID and its preferences.",
    expires: "1 year",
  },
  {
    name: "_clsk",
    party: "First-party",
    purpose: "Connects the pages you view into a single recorded session.",
    expires: "1 day",
  },
  {
    name: "CLID",
    party: "Third-party (clarity.ms)",
    purpose: "Records the first time Clarity saw this browser on any website that uses Clarity.",
    expires: "1 year",
  },
  {
    name: "MUID",
    party: "Third-party (Microsoft)",
    purpose: "Identifies unique browsers visiting Microsoft websites.",
    expires: "1 year",
  },
  {
    name: "MR",
    party: "Third-party (Microsoft)",
    purpose: "Indicates whether to refresh the MUID.",
    expires: "7 days",
  },
  {
    name: "SM",
    party: "Third-party (Microsoft)",
    purpose: "Synchronizes the MUID across Microsoft domains.",
    expires: "End of session",
  },
  {
    name: "ANONCHK",
    party: "Third-party (Microsoft)",
    purpose: "Technical flag; Clarity always sets it to 0.",
    expires: "10 minutes",
  },
];

const accessibilityStorage = [
  {
    name: "negishot_prefs",
    type: "Cookie (first-party)",
    purpose: "Remembers the accessibility settings you chose.",
    expires: "30 days",
  },
  {
    name: "negishot_prefs_<code>",
    type: "Local storage",
    purpose: "Remembers the accessibility settings you chose.",
    expires: "Until you clear it",
  },
  {
    name: "negishot_sid",
    type: "Local storage",
    purpose: "A random ID that groups your use of the widget into a session for Negishot's usage statistics.",
    expires: "Until you clear it",
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Tal Israeli"
  description="How Tal Israeli's personal website, talisrae.li, handles your information, including the optional Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity analytics."
>
  <fieldset>
    <legend>Privacy Policy</legend>
    <p class="updated">
      Last updated:{" "}
      <time datetime={lastUpdated.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}>
        {lastUpdated.toLocaleDateString("en-US", { year: "numeric", month: "long", day: "numeric", timeZone: "UTC" })}
      </time>
    </p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>talisrae.li</strong> (the &ldquo;Website&rdquo;), the personal website of
      Tal Israeli (&ldquo;I&rdquo;, &ldquo;me&rdquo; or &ldquo;my&rdquo;), handles information about you. The short
      version: the Website has no accounts and no ads, and I do not sell your information. With your permission only, it
      uses Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity to understand how visitors use it.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information Stored on Your Device</h2>
    <p>
      The Website saves two things in your browser's local storage: your theme (light or dark) and your cookie choice,
      so they stay the same on your next visit. These values stay on your device and are never sent to me. The
      accessibility widget can also save your accessibility settings, as described in section 3. You can remove all of
      them at any time by clearing your browser's site data.
    </p>

    <h2 id="analytics">2. Analytics and Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      The Website uses two analytics services, but only if you allow them. Until you choose, and if you decline, neither
      service is loaded and no analytics cookies are set. Each one can be allowed or declined on its own, and declining
      does not affect how the Website works.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can change or withdraw your choice at any time from{" "}
      <button type="button" class="link" data-action="help-cookies">
        Manage Cookies
      </button>{" "}
      (also in the footer and in the &ldquo;Help&rdquo; menu). When you withdraw a choice, the Website deletes that
      service's cookies from your browser.
    </p>

    <h3>2.1. Google Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      Google Analytics, provided by Google LLC, helps me count visits and see which pages are read. When you allow it,
      it collects:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>the pages you visit, their titles, and the website or link that brought you here;</li>
      <li>how you engage with pages, such as time spent, scrolling and clicks on links to other websites;</li>
      <li>your device type, operating system, browser, screen size and language;</li>
      <li>
        your approximate location (country, region and city), derived from your IP address. For visitors from the EU,
        the UK and Switzerland, Google uses the IP address only to derive this location and then discards it, without
        logging or storing it;
      </li>
      <li>a random identifier, stored in the cookies below, that recognizes your browser between visits.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      I have turned off Google signals and ad personalization, so this data is not linked to your Google account and is
      not used for advertising. Event-level data is deleted automatically after 2 months; I keep only aggregated reports
      after that.
    </p>
    <table>
      <caption>Google Analytics cookies (first-party, set on talisrae.li)</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Cookie</th>
          <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
          <th scope="col">Expires</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {googleAnalyticsCookies.map((cookie) => (
          <tr>
            <td>
              <code>{cookie.name}</code>
            </td>
            <td>{cookie.purpose}</td>
            <td>{cookie.expires}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Learn more in the{" "}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Google Privacy Policy
      </a>{" "}
      and{" "}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        how Google uses information from sites that use its services
      </a>
      . You can also block Google Analytics on all websites with the{" "}
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h3>2.2. Microsoft Clarity</h3>
    <p>
      Microsoft Clarity, provided by Microsoft Corporation, shows me how pages are used through heatmaps and session
      recordings. A recording is not a video: it is a reconstruction of the page from what you saw and what you did on
      it. When you allow it, Clarity collects:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>your interactions with pages, such as mouse movements, clicks, taps and scrolling;</li>
      <li>
        the content of the pages as they appeared to you (the Website has no forms, and text typed into input fields is
        always masked);
      </li>
      <li>the pages you visit and the website or link that brought you here;</li>
      <li>your device type, operating system, browser and screen size;</li>
      <li>your approximate location (country), derived from your IP address;</li>
      <li>a random identifier, stored in the cookies below, that recognizes your browser between visits.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Session recordings are kept for up to 30 days, except for a small number that I or Clarity save, which are kept
      for up to 9 months. Heatmaps are available for up to 9 months. Clarity's data is stored in Microsoft Azure,
      Microsoft acts as an independent controller of it, and Microsoft does not sell it. Clarity respects the Global
      Privacy Control (GPC) signal. The Website allows Clarity analytics storage only; Microsoft advertising storage
      stays denied.
    </p>
    <table>
      <caption>Microsoft Clarity cookies</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Cookie</th>
          <th scope="col">Type</th>
          <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
          <th scope="col">Expires</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {clarityCookies.map((cookie) => (
          <tr>
            <td>
              <code>{cookie.name}</code>
            </td>
            <td>{cookie.party}</td>
            <td>{cookie.purpose}</td>
            <td>{cookie.expires}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Learn more in the{" "}
      <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Microsoft Privacy Statement
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2 id="accessibility">3. Accessibility Widget</h2>
    <p>
      To make the Website accessible, it includes an accessibility widget provided by Negishot (negishot.co.il). It lets
      you adjust things like text size, spacing, colors and contrast. Because it is needed for accessibility, it is
      loaded on every page and does not depend on your cookie choice.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Loading the widget sends Negishot the standard technical information of any web request, such as your IP
        address, browser type and the page you are on.
      </li>
      <li>
        When you open the widget, it loads its fonts from Google Fonts, jsDelivr and getmood.io, which receive the same
        kind of technical information.
      </li>
      <li>
        When you use one of its tools, it sends Negishot which tool you used, together with a random session ID, for
        usage statistics. It does not send the content of the pages or anything you type.
      </li>
      <li>
        When you change a setting, it saves your settings on your device, so they stay the same on your next visit.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <table>
      <caption>Accessibility widget storage</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Name</th>
          <th scope="col">Type</th>
          <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
          <th scope="col">Expires</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {accessibilityStorage.map((item) => (
          <tr>
            <td>
              <code>{item.name}</code>
            </td>
            <td>{item.type}</td>
            <td>{item.purpose}</td>
            <td>{item.expires}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      The widget does not use this information for advertising or to track you across websites. To reset your settings,
      use the widget's reset option or clear your browser's site data. For more information, see{" "}
      <a href="https://negishot.co.il" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        negishot.co.il
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2>4. Hosting and Server Logs</h2>
    <p>
      The Website is hosted on Microsoft Azure Static Web Apps. Like most web hosts, Microsoft may automatically process
      technical information when your browser requests a page, such as your IP address, browser type, the page requested
      and the time of the request, in order to deliver the Website and keep it secure. I do not use this information to
      identify you. Microsoft handles it according to the{" "}
      <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Microsoft Privacy Statement
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2>5. When You Contact Me</h2>
    <p>
      If you email me or reach out through LinkedIn, GitHub or X, I will receive the information you choose to send,
      such as your name, email address and message. I use it only to reply to you and continue our conversation, and I
      keep it only as long as needed for that purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Third-Party Websites</h2>
    <p>
      The Website links to other websites, including LinkedIn, GitHub, X, Facebook, WhatsApp and the sources cited in my
      projects. The options in the &ldquo;Share&rdquo; and &ldquo;Connect&rdquo; menus simply open those websites in a
      new tab; nothing is sent to them until you open them. Once you do, their own privacy policies apply, and I am not
      responsible for how they handle your information.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Legal Basis and International Transfers</h2>
    <p>
      I use Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity only on the basis of your consent, which you can withdraw at any time
      without affecting the lawfulness of what was collected before. The accessibility widget is used because it is
      necessary to make the Website accessible to everyone, and it stores your settings only when you ask it to. Google
      and Microsoft may process this data in the United States and other countries where they operate, under the
      safeguards described in their privacy policies.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Website is not directed at children, and I do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under the
      age of 16.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct or delete personal information about you,
      to object to how it is used, and to complain to a data protection authority. You can withdraw your analytics
      consent at any time from Manage Cookies. Analytics data is identified only by a random ID in your browser, so I
      usually cannot link it to you; to make any other request, email me at the address below and I will respond within
      a reasonable time.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      I may update this Privacy Policy from time to time, for example if the Website gains new features. The updated
      version will be posted on this page with a new &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date. If I add a new analytics service,
      I will ask for your permission again.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please email me at{" "}
      <a href="mailto:contact@talisrae.li">contact@talisrae.li</a>. See also the{" "}
      <a href="/terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a>.
    </p>
  </fieldset>
</Layout>

<style lang="scss">
  .updated {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 1rem 0 0.25rem;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0.25rem;
  }

  fieldset p {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
  }

  ul {
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
  }

  button.link {
    padding: 0;
    border: none;
    background: none;
    color: var(--link-color);
    font: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  // Like the tables on the Education page.
  table {
    width: 100%;
    margin-block-start: 0.5rem;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    border: var(--window-border) 1px solid;
    font-size: 0.85rem;

    caption {
      text-align: start;
      font-weight: 500;
      padding-block-end: 0.25rem;
    }

    th,
    td {
      padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
      border: var(--window-border) 1px solid;
      text-align: start;
      vertical-align: top;
    }

    th {
      background: var(--tab-button-inactive-bg);
      font-weight: 500;
    }

    code {
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
  }
</style>
